          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माता (mātā) — \"mother\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The stem is मातृ (mātṛ-) — the same -ṛ family as पिता (pitā), and the same long reach: Latin māter, Greek mētēr, Old English mōdor, English mother, Russian mat. Put the father-word into the dual and Sanskrit gives you pitarau, 'the two parents', with the mother folded silently inside it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two of the four, and one ending family carrying both."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
