    {
      "id": "SA-S222-vowel-sign-uu",
      "sequence": 1121,
      "title": "◌ू (ū) — one character, met inside words you already say",
      "headword": "ू",
      "romanization": "ū",
      "gloss": "the single character ◌ू — recognised inside words you already say",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "writing-block",
        "script-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:34008d6789eb5c6c",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Script you'll notice: ◌ू",
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on and your eyes, for letter shapes on the page. You can listen to everything else now — leave the sections called Script you'll notice: ◌ू and Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one, the ones you have already met: श, छ, ड. Say what each of them does."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One character this time. One only — and you have been saying it for pages without knowing which mark on the page it was."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ◌ू",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "◌ू — ū."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is a vowel sign. It is not a letter and never stands alone: it attaches to a consonant and replaces the a built into it. Replaces, not adds — the a is gone."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where it sits: a longer hook below the consonant."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Worked through: न + ◌ू = नू — nū."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already say these, and every one of them has ◌ू (ū) somewhere inside it:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सूनुः sūnuḥ — son."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ◌ू — copy what you see",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put your pen on ◌ू (ū) and follow its line. Copy the shape you can see — slowly, and larger than it is printed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This book does not yet tell you where to start the character or which way to travel. That is a real thing, taught with real variation from school to school, and it is not written down here until it can be written down with a source. Copying what is in front of you needs no such source, and it is how the shape gets into your hand in the meantime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at this, and find ◌ू (ū) in it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at this, and find ◌ू in it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सूनुः (sūnuḥ)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "TRACE",
              "instruction": "◌ू three times, saying ū as you finish each one",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU TRACE: ◌ू three times, saying *ū* as you finish each one]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "back at any page of this chapter and find ◌ू (ū) once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: back at any page of this chapter and find ◌ू once more]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which character is this — ◌ू? What vowel does it put on the consonant it attaches to — and what does it take off? (Puts ū on; takes the built-in a off.) Name one word you already say that contains it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
